## KDP interior PDF requirements

### File itself

* **PDF required for Hebrew**.
* **Maximum 650 MB**.
* **Single pages**, not spreads/2-up.
* **Do not encrypt/lock** the PDF.
* Page dimensions must exactly match the selected **trim size + bleed, if any**.  

### Strip this stuff out

KDP says the submitted PDF should not contain:

* crop marks
* trim marks
* bookmarks
* comments
* annotations
* invisible objects
* placeholder text
* unnecessary metadata
* printer's marks 

### Fonts

* **Embed every font.**
* Amazon recommends **fully embedded**, rather than subset-embedded fonts. 

This is one of the things I'd investigate hardest with our insane collection of fonts.

### Images / graphics

* Embed all images.
* Images should be **≥300 DPI**.
* Flatten transparent objects and layers.
* Don't downsample images when making the print PDF.  

### PDF flavor

Amazon recommends:

> **PDF/X; PDF/X-1a preferred.**

Also optimize the PDF, but **don't reduce image resolution**. 

This is probably the most useful new information from your Ctrl+A. **Having Codex generate a clean PDF/X-1a KDP artifact from our LuaLaTeX output is a very sensible target.**

### Layout things relevant to us

* Lines should be at least **0.75 pt / 0.01"** thick.
* All pages should have the same orientation.
* Text should generally be at least **7 pt**.
* Nothing should overlap or be cut off.
* No more than **4 consecutive blank pages** at the beginning/middle or **10 at the end**.  

